Democratic Socialist Arab Ba'ath Party\",\"Democratic Socialist Unionist Party\",\"Democratic capitalism\",\"Democratic republic\",\"Democratization\",\"Dennis Skinner\",\"Deposition (politics)\",\"Derek Hatton\",\"Dersim rebellion\",\"Dhofar rebellion\",\"Dick Taverne\",\"Dirty War\",\"Discourse on Inequality\",\"Discourses Concerning Government\",\"Discourses on Livy\",\"Dissolution of Czechoslovakia\",\"Dissolution of the Soviet Union\",\"Division of Korea\",\"Doi (identifier)\",\"Dominican Civil War\",\"Domino theory\",\"Doug Naysmith\",\"Downtown Amman\",\"Dutch Republic\",\"Dwight D. Eisenhower\",\"Détente\",\"Eagle of Saladin\",\"East German uprising of 1953\",\"Eastern Bloc\",\"Egalitarianism\",\"Egypt\",\"Egyptian Crisis (2011–2014)\",\"Egyptian Revolution of 1952\",\"Egyptian nationalism\",\"Egyptian revolution of 1952\",\"Egyptian–Libyan War\",\"Eisenhower Doctrine\",\"El Porteñazo\",\"Eleftherios Venizelos\",\"Elias Farah\",\"Elin Jones\",\"Ellen Schrecker\",\"Eritrean Civil Wars\",\"Eritrean War of Independence\",\"Ethel Mannin\",\"Ethiopian Civil War\",\"Ethnic nationalism\",\"Eurocommunism\",\"European Economic Community\",\"Fadil Mahmud Gharib\",\"Fahd Jassem al-Freij\",\"Faisal I\",\"Faisal II of Iraq\",\"Faith Campaign\",\"Falklands War\",\"Fall of communism in Albania\",\"Fall of the Assad regime\",\"Fall of the Berlin Wall\",\"Fall of the inner German border\",\"Farouk al-Sharaa\",\"Fascism\",\"Fatah\",\"Fatah–Hamas conflict\",\"Fawzi Mutlaq al-Rawi\",\"Fedayeen Saddam\",\"Federal republic\",\"Federation of Arab Republics\",\"Fertile Crescent\",\"Festa della Repubblica\",\"Fidelismo\",\"Finlandization\",\"First Indochina War\",\"First Intifada\",\"First Iraqi–Kurdish War\",\"First Nagorno-Karabakh War\",\"First Taiwan Strait Crisis\",\"First Yemenite War\",\"Flag of the Arab Federation\",\"Flag of the Arab Revolt\",\"Flag of the Federation of Arab Republics\",\"Flag of the United Arab Republic\",\"Forces of Freedom and Change\",\"Four Power Agreement on Berlin\",\"Franco-Syrian War\",\"Franco-Turkish War\",\"Fred Halliday\",\"Free Iraqi Army\",\"Free Officers Movement (Egypt)\",\"French Revolution\",\"French Revolution of 1848\",\"Front of Patriotic and National Parties\",\"Frozen conflict\",\"Fuad al-Rikabi\",\"Gabriel Gorodetsky\",\"Gabriel Kolko\",\"Gamal Abdel Nasser\",\"Gar Alperovitz\",\"Gaullism\",\"Gaza war\",\"Gaṇasaṅgha\",\"Geir Lundestad\",\"General Federation of Trade Unions (Syria)\"],\"blacklist\":[],\"lastLinkClicked\":\"14 July Revolution\"},\"ladderLevel\":0.27683640574638513,\"innerBudgetRemaining\":99.65000000000002,\"probeResult\":{\"pass\":true,\"results\":[]},\"isStable\":false,\"action\":{\"type\":\"NAVIGATE\",\"title\":\"French Revolution\"},\"next\":{\"currentTitle\":\"French Revolution\",\"summary\":\"The French Revolution was a period of political and societal change in France that began with the Estates General of 1789 and ended with the Coup of 18 Brumaire on 9 November 1799. Many of the revolution's ideas are considered fundamental principles of liberal democracy, and its values remain central to modern French political discourse. It was caused by a combination of social, political, and economic factors which the existing regime proved unable to manage.  \\nFinancial crisis and widespread social distress led to the convocation of the Estates General in May 1789, its first meeting since 1614. The representatives of the Third Estate broke away and re-constituted themselves as a National Assembly in June. The Storming of the Bastille in Paris on 14 July led to a series of radical measures by the Assembly, including the abolition of feudalism, state control over the Catholic Church in France, and issuing the Declaration of the Rights of Man and of the Citizen. \\nThe next three years were dominated by a struggle for political control. King Louis XVI's attempted flight to Varennes in June 1791 further discredited the monarchy, and military defeats after the outbreak of the French Revolutionary Wars in April 1792 led to the insurrection of 10 August 1792. As a result, the monarchy was replaced by the French First Republic in September, followed by the execution of Louis XVI himself in January 1793.\\nAfter another revolt in June 1793, the constitution was suspended, and political power passed from the National Convention to the Committee of Public Safety, dominated by radical Jacobins led by Maximilien Robespierre. About 16,000 people were sentenced by the Revolutionary Tribunal and executed in the Reign of Terror, which ended in July 1794 with the Thermidorian Reaction. Weakened by external threats and internal opposition, the Committee of Public Safety was replaced in November 1795 by the Directory. Its instability ended in 1799 with the coup of 18 Brumaire and the establishment of the Consulate, with Napoleon Bonaparte as First Consul.\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French%20Revolution\",\"goal\":\"French Revolution\",\"history\":[\"American Revolution\",\"14 July Revolution\",\"French Revolution\"],\"depth\":3,\"links\":[\"11 September 1922 Revolution\",\"13 Vendémiaire\",\"14 July Revolution\",\"1791 French legislative election\",\"1792 French National Convention election\",\"1795 French legislative election\",\"1798 French legislative election\",\"1851 French coup d'état\",\"18 Brumaire\",\"1911 Revolution\",\"1935 Greek coup d'état attempt\",\"1946 Italian institutional referendum\",\"1952 Egyptian revolution\",\"1960 South African republic referendum\",\"1969 Libyan coup d'état\",\"1970 Cambodian coup d'état\",\"1987 Fijian coups d'état\",\"2005 French riots\",\"2010 Kyrgyz Revolution\",\"2011 Egyptian revolution\",\"2017 French presidential election\",\"2021 French labor protests\",\"2022 French presidential election\",\"2022 Russian invasion of Ukraine\",\"5 October 1910 revolution\",\"A Discourse on the Love of Our Country\",\"A Vindication of the Rights of Men\",\"Abolition of feudalism in France\",\"Abolition of monarchy